{"title":"Career Roadmap · AYUSH Medical Officer","role":"AYUSH Medical Officer","summary":"An AYUSH Medical Officer (Naturopathy & Yoga) provides healthcare services within the scope of naturopathy and yoga, typically in AYUSH hospitals, wellness centres, dispensaries, government health programmes, integrative-care settings, and related institutions.","facts":{"Current degree":"BNYS (Naturopathy & Yogic Sciences)","Course":"Naturopathy & Yoga"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An AYUSH Medical Officer (Naturopathy & Yoga) provides healthcare services within the scope of naturopathy and yoga, typically in AYUSH hospitals, wellness centres, dispensaries, government health programmes, integrative-care settings, and related institutions."},{"type":"h","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"h","text":"Naturopathic approaches"},{"type":"h","text":"Yoga-based health and wellness interventions"},{"type":"h","text":"Lifestyle and preventive healthcare"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient assessment and documentation"},{"type":"h","text":"Health education and counselling"},{"type":"h","text":"Public-health activities"},{"type":"h","text":"Referral and coordination with conventional healthcare when required"},{"type":"p","text":"The practitioner should be trained to recognize medical emergencies and refer patients appropriately, rather than delaying necessary conventional medical care."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"10+2 / Intermediate"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"├── Physics"},{"type":"h","text":"├── Chemistry"},{"type":"h","text":"└── Biology"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"▼"},{"type":"h","text":"NEET-UG / Applicable Admission Route"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"▼"},{"type":"h","text":"BNYS – Bachelor of Naturopathy"},{"type":"h","text":"& Yogic Sciences"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"▼"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Training /"},{"type":"h","text":"Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"▼"},{"type":"h","text":"Professional Registration /"},{"type":"h","text":"Applicable Eligibility"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"▼"},{"type":"h","text":"AYUSH Medical Officer"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"┌─────┼──────────────┐"},{"type":"h","text":"▼ ▼ ▼"},{"type":"h","text":"Govt. AYUSH Wellness /"},{"type":"h","text":"Health Hospital Integrative"},{"type":"h","text":"Services Healthcare"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"▼"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Medical Officer /"},{"type":"h","text":"Administrative / Specialist /"},{"type":"h","text":"Public Health Roles"},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"Government recruitment, professional registration, designation, and eligibility requirements can vary by state, department, institution, and recruitment notification. Students should verify the current official requirements before applying."}]},{"heading":"BNYS Academic Roadmap","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Medical & Foundational Sciences"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on understanding the human body and the foundations of naturopathy and yoga."},{"type":"h","text":"Core Areas"},{"type":"h","text":"Human Anatomy"},{"type":"h","text":"Human Physiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Biochemistry"},{"type":"h","text":"Yoga fundamentals"},{"type":"h","text":"Naturopathic philosophy"},{"type":"h","text":"Basic nutrition"},{"type":"h","text":"Introduction to health and disease"},{"type":"h","text":"Basic clinical observation"},{"type":"h","text":"Skills to Develop"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient communication"},{"type":"h","text":"Basic clinical documentation"},{"type":"h","text":"Health history taking"},{"type":"h","text":"Basic vital-sign assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Scientific reading"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical terminology"},{"type":"h","text":"Professional ethics"},{"type":"h","text":"Suggested Activities"},{"type":"h","text":"Anatomy revision using 3D resources"},{"type":"h","text":"Yoga practice log"},{"type":"h","text":"Nutrition diary analysis"},{"type":"h","text":"Community health observation"},{"type":"h","text":"Basic case-history documentation"}]},{"heading":"Year 2 — Naturopathy & Clinical Foundations","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The student begins connecting biomedical knowledge with naturopathic and yogic approaches."},{"type":"h","text":"Major Learning Areas"},{"type":"h","text":"Naturopathic therapies"},{"type":"h","text":"Yoga therapy"},{"type":"h","text":"Nutrition and dietetics"},{"type":"h","text":"Pathology"},{"type":"h","text":"Microbiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmacology fundamentals"},{"type":"h","text":"Psychology"},{"type":"h","text":"Community medicine"},{"type":"h","text":"Basic clinical assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Practical Skills"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient interview"},{"type":"h","text":"Lifestyle assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Diet assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Yoga practice planning"},{"type":"h","text":"Basic therapeutic procedure preparation"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient education"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical record maintenance"},{"type":"h","text":"Example Case Exercise"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient History"},{"type":"h","text":"Lifestyle Assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Basic Clinical Assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Identify Health Concerns"},{"type":"h","text":"Determine Appropriate Naturopathy /"},{"type":"h","text":"Yoga Intervention"},{"type":"h","text":"Monitor Response"},{"type":"h","text":"Modify / Refer When Required"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Clinical Naturopathy & Yoga"},{"type":"p","text":"The emphasis shifts toward supervised clinical practice."},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Areas"},{"type":"h","text":"General medicine"},{"type":"h","text":"Naturopathic clinical practice"},{"type":"h","text":"Yoga therapy"},{"type":"h","text":"Diet therapy"},{"type":"h","text":"Hy